.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# credential files EAS needs at submit time (see secrets/README.md)
secrets/*
!secrets/README.md

# google-services.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds no secret — no private
# key, no token — and it is compiled into every APK by design, so it cannot be one.
# Ignoring it would only mean EAS (which builds from the git archive) never receives
# it, and push would fail silently on every Android build. The Firebase API key in it
# is a client identifier; it is protected by restricting it to the package name and
# signing certificate in the Google Cloud console, not by hiding the file.
